&lt;p&gt;WSP 84: 1989-99. WSP 1509: 1902, 1939(M). WSP 1559: Drainage area. WSP 1709: 1953, 1956-57. The maximum gage height for water year 2017 was revised on July 24, 2021,&nbsp; based on reanalysis of gage height data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gage datum was revised on Oct. 2, 2026, because the previous NAVD88 datum was found to be in error based on the Level II GNSS survey performed by USGS on Dec. 3, 2024.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;WDR MT-2013: Drainage area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The water year 2025 peak gage height and discharge were revised on June 25, 2026, following a re-evaluation of the record.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Site visit reference readings and discharge measurement mean gage heights were revised for the June 11, 2025, August 19, 2025, and November 19, 2025, visits&nbsp;on June 25, 2026, following a re-evaluation of the record.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;WDR MT-2013: Drainage area. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The maximum discharge and gage height for water year 2010 along with gage height and discharge for the period June 21, 2010 to Oct. 31, 2010, were revised on August 6, 2021, based upon reanalysis of data.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The maximum discharge for water year 2024 was revised on March 2, 2026 to add peak qualification code 6 to the reading.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Water Supply Paper (WSP) 1309: 1912, 1915 (maximum discharge), 1918, 1925. WSP 1729: Drainage area. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The maximum gage height affected by backwater for water year 2009 was removed on September 7, 2021, based on reanalysis of data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The datum was revised on January 31, 2025 because the previous NGVD29 datum was found to be in error based on the Level II GNSS survey that was performed by USGS on August 8, 2024.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;WDR MT-2013: Drainage area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Measurement on Nov. 8, 2021 was determined to not be relative to the stage discharge relationship; the flow did not reach the control and was below the GZF.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The estimated discharge from Nov. 7-18, 2021 was determined to be zero flow.&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mean gage height for measurement #202 (July 17, 2023) was changed from 2.11 ft to 2.09 ft on Feb. 20, 2024 due to change in gage height correction.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Daily mean values of discharge, water year peaks of gage height, and water year peaks of discharge from 1932 to 1986, originally published under this station, were moved to station 06209510 - Rock Creek above Mourice Creek, near Red Lodge, MT, on July 26, 2023.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wyoming
StreamStats 2025: Drainage area.&lt;/p&gt;

