10, 2020, were revised on Mar. 2, 2020, based on datum correction from levels.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 7.5pt; background: white;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; color: black;"&gt;Gage height and discharge for the period of Oct. 1, 2019 to Feb. 23, 2021, were revised on Mar. 29, 2021, based on datum correction from levels.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 7.5pt; background: white;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; color: black;"&gt;Gage heights assigned to measured discharges were revised for measurements 938 to 964 on Mar. 29, 2021 as indicated by datum correction analysis on level surveys performed Feb. 20 2020 and Feb. 24, 2021.&nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
